# NOTICE

## Security notice — sensitive capability

**This project extracts and decrypts another application's login credentials.**

Specifically, to sign in automatically without restarting the client, it reads the
running WorkBuddy desktop client process memory, locates the key material,
decrypts the login-state envelope, and obtains `accessToken` / `refreshToken` /
`idToken`. Extracted credentials are equivalent to your session — a leak means
account takeover. Reading another application's process memory may also conflict
with that application's terms of service.

**Read [`SECURITY.md`](SECURITY.md) before use.** Use only with your own account,
on a personal device you trust.

The build published on the WorkBuddy platform does **not** contain this capability;
it provides cloud check-in and self-healing only.

## Reverse engineering

This project automates the WorkBuddy "Buddy Station" daily check-in.
The API surface was reverse-engineered from the WorkBuddy desktop client and
is not officially documented — endpoints, headers and error codes may change
in any client update.

You are responsible for:
  - complying with the terms of service of the services you automate;
  - keeping your own credentials (AirScript-Token, refresh tokens) private —
    the repository ships empty templates, never commit real values;
  - setting appropriate permissions on any sheet that stores a token;
  - accepting the risks listed in `SECURITY.md`, including the risk that
    credentials extracted from process memory are compromised.

